const variables=[
  ['Width, height, streams','Pixels and independent camera views per decision','Read active sensor output and crop/resize configuration; count each stream after preprocessing.','A megapixel count does not reveal field of view, optics, occlusion, or small-target contrast.'],
  ['Frame rate, frame history','How often input arrives and how many frames one decision can use','Use captured timestamps, dropped-frame logs and the actual temporal buffer.','Correlated adjacent frames are not independent training examples.'],
  ['Critical feature span','Smallest task-relevant cue in the input image, in pixels','Measure labeled target boxes/keypoints at the farthest required range and worst allowed conditions.','The same physical object changes pixel size with range, focal length and crop.'],
  ['Patch/token unit','Pixels mapped to one visual token in the proposed representation','Inspect the actual tokenizer or feature pyramid and its output shapes.','Patch size alone does not prove information loss; learned embeddings can retain subpatch detail.'],
  ['Context X','Maximum input tokens available in one inference window','Read the deployed model/configuration; log truncation and frame selection.','Capacity can be lost to other modalities, masks, caches and reserved tokens.'],
  ['Output steps Z','Autoregressive tokens or iterative actions per decision','Count the actual decode/rollout steps and tool invocations in traces.','A one-pass detector has no meaningful autoregressive Z; use measured pipeline work instead.'],
  ['Task factors Y','Proposed number of independently varying causal or label-relevant factors','Design controlled dataset interventions and see which factors independently change the correct output.','Current UI Y is an ordinal hypothesis proxy, not a measured intrinsic dimension.'],
  ['Composition depth','Proposed levels of reusable subrules needed for the task','Specify a primitive vocabulary, fit a task-conditional grammar, and measure held-out predictive gain.','Different primitive vocabularies give different depths.'],
  ['Motif reuse','How often a useful subrule recurs across task examples','Count repeated task-relevant motifs after deduplication and context stratification.','Repeated pixels or duplicate files are not necessarily repeated useful rules.'],
  ['Tail novelty','Share of evaluation cases requiring unseen combinations or mechanisms','Predefine scenario taxonomy, measure out-of-distribution distance and slice prevalence.','There is no universal scalar novelty meter; preserve the actual scenario labels.'],
  ['Independent examples','Effective coverage of distinct task situations in training','Cluster near-duplicates, groups, sources, subjects and trajectories; report group counts and exposures.','Raw image/frame/token count can greatly overstate independent evidence.'],
  ['Anchor and targets','Measured model/score anchor and requested ordinary/tail operating points','Run a frozen architecture family at several sizes and data budgets on a fixed, held-out protocol.','A single anchor cannot identify a scaling exponent; accuracy is not a safety probability.'],
  ['Model size P, weight bits','Number of stored parameters and representation precision','Inspect deployment artifact and quantization metadata; compute P × bits ÷ 8.','Weight bytes omit activations, KV, code, redundancy and fragmentation.'],
  ['Effective compute','Sustained arithmetic rate for the exact workload and precision','Benchmark on the target device, batch size and thermal regime.','Peak TOPS, sparse TOPS and FP TFLOP/s are not interchangeable.'],
  ['Effective bandwidth','Sustained bytes/s for the model traffic pattern','Profile actual tensor movement, cache reuse and concurrent sensor/pipeline loads.','Published DRAM bandwidth is an upper bound, not delivered bandwidth.'],
  ['Deadline L','Latest useful decision time, from sensing to action','Allocate capture, transfer, preprocessing, inference, fusion, planning, actuation and margin.','Average FPS can pass while rare latency spikes miss deadlines.'],
];
